Changes: original Rust serializers, batched CPU formatting/transposition,
GPU history capture, primitive-array resident checkpoint envelope and C ABI.
No withdrawn WRF-Hydro code, schemas, fixtures or native runtime are used.

The NetCDF container calls use netCDF-C. The default developer build links
the system library; build_local_backend.py statically links pinned local-file
netCDF-C 4.9.3 (3a6b1debf1557f07b606ce3653e44f0d711203be), HDF5 1.14.6
(7bf340440909d468dbb3cf41f0ea0d87f5050cea), and zlib 1.3.1
(51b7f2abdade71cd9bb0e7a373ef2610ec6f9daf). Archive and licence hashes
are in backend-sources.json. NETCDF-C-NOTICE retains the netCDF grant;
netCDF-Fortran is not linked or shipped.
NetCDF-4 uses netCDF-C's HDF5 C backend; its full HDF5/LBNL grants are
retained in HDF5-NOTICE.txt. This is not a pure-Rust NetCDF-4 container.
ZLIB-NOTICE.txt and UTF8PROC-NOTICE.txt retain the zlib, bundled utf8proc
and processed Unicode-data grants. The C source files are unmodified.

Parquet container: Apache Arrow parquet-rs 56.2.0, Apache-2.0.
Its complete Apache notice is retained in PARQUET-NOTICE.txt.
Snappy-Rust snap 1.1.2 is BSD-3-Clause; SNAP-NOTICE.txt retains its notice.
No Apache/Pandas/PyArrow creator identity is claimed for ArWen-generated files.
